  biomeName: The Granite Spine
  minDepthMeters: -200
  maxDepthMeters: 0
  shortDescription: A continuous obsidian-smooth vertical wall marking the end of
    the sea.
  isPlaceholder: 0
  visitPurpose: Early exploration biome. Come here to learn routes, gather basics,
    and read walls, fissures, and major vertical routes.
  commonRewardHook: Common runs pay out in Sulfur Clumps and Thermal Gel.
  rareRewardHook: 'Rare pull is modest: Tungsten Chunk and Cooling Cartridge.'
  landmarkIdentity: The Granite Spine reads through walls, fins, fissures, and giant
    vertical breaks. Landmarks should feel bright and readable.
  safePocketIdentity: Safe pockets are frequent. The player should often see a clear
    reset point nearby.
  riskSummary: 'Main failure mode: vertical trap geometry and hard commitment. Creature
    pressure stays high.'
  extractionFocus: 'Quick strike extraction from hot pockets with short exposure
    windows. Early tier: keep runs short and work edges, cracks, and vertical seams.'
  landmarkGuidance: Dominant landmark is heat vent field or obsidian flow edge. This
    slot should read through glass lip, vent mouth, or hot crack; use walls and breaks
    to mark route commitment.
